# The fingerprint HAL walks this subtree during startup. It could do so before
# this repo existed, because leds@d300 was left with the default sysfs label
# and hal_fingerprint_default may search that. Narrowing the subtree to
# sysfs_flash_led in genfs_contexts took the access away and cost it three
# denials on every boot, so it is given back explicitly.
#
# It reads modalias out of the subtree while enumerating devices, so this needs
# the file read as well as the directory search. Granting only the search moves
# the denial along one step rather than fixing it, which is exactly what
# happened the first time round.
allow hal_fingerprint_default sysfs_flash_led:dir search;
allow hal_fingerprint_default sysfs_flash_led:file r_file_perms;
